{"title":"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_17\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 17</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(AMC_10_Bijection)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (AMC 10 Bijection)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_17\">Problem 17</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 17\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Four students are seated in a row. They chat with the people sitting next to them, then rearrange themselves so that they are no longer seated next to any of the same people. How many rearrangements are possible?\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2026_amc_8_q17.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/4a/2026_amc_8_q17.png/650px-2026_amc_8_q17.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"650\" height=\"231\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/4/4a/2026_amc_8_q17.png 1.5x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87efe1cfd7636b86720f1ae429244fa7653b1951.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 4 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 9 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 12 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"369\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28AMC_10_Bijection.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(AMC_10_Bijection)\">Solution 1 (AMC 10 Bijection)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (AMC 10 Bijection)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Label the human beings A, B, C, and D in that order from left to right. It doesn't matter the original configuration. Now, the problem is:\n</p><p>How many four letter strings ABCD exist such that A is not next to B, B not next to C, and C is not next to D.\n</p><p>We can count the number of strings manually (or just do casework), to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e8656291085c388b48a0fa8da85aed21c483bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><b>Remarks:</b>\n</p>\n<ul><li>This is incredibly similar to one AMC 10 problem, that asked how many four letter strings abcd have no two consecutive letters in the alphabet next to one another.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Derangements cannot work here as you require <i>linear non-adjacencies</i></li></ul>\n<p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's say the people are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and they seated in the order <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> at first. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be next to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be next to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be next to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, so our only possibilities are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2a2246ef08c3b38ff7d9aec215e4789279c53c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CADB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/531e7128308b99ef0ea70212f84059203f1681f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> as orders, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/5/47537e9d7cc9fc2e4e84976e3643ebe3b95b0967.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathbf{(A) 2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"54\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~Yuhao2012\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> sits next to both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> can only sit next to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. The only way this is possible is if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> sits at either the front or the back. We can apply this same logic to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/792daa030c96693198f143f9176bf888b7ca25cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C.$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> There are now two cases: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/531e7128308b99ef0ea70212f84059203f1681f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/2/1d2325a84fdd55c6523d8f49a7a0d5c1b39bb7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CADB,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> which is the former with its order reversed. Therefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/0/ae021a11b3a707bd338bc14e34c125e6d883bfad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(A)} 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"52\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~clever14710owl\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Screenshot_2026-10-17_104441.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/6a/Screenshot_2026-10-17_104441.png/523px-Screenshot_2026-10-17_104441.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"523\" height=\"328\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/6a/Screenshot_2026-10-17_104441.png/785px-Screenshot_2026-10-17_104441.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/6/6a/Screenshot_2026-10-17_104441.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n~Aarnavisthebest\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gzXlOkLl24U\">https://youtu.be/gzXlOkLl24U</a>\n</p><p>~TheSmartGreekMathDude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nY1hhVbEeBk\">https://youtu.be/nY1hhVbEeBk</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Thinking Feet\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Euy6mP9oV_U\">https://youtu.be/Euy6mP9oV_U</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YJnsl4zjdK8\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YJnsl4zjdK8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=1913s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=1913s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1UcNx6KEo9/\">https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1UcNx6KEo9/</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody